[
  {
    "group": "How it runs",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "The gateway has Spring Cloud Gateway routes for vets-service, visits-service, customers-service and genai-service, each using an <code>lb://</code> service-name URI and a path prefix of <code>/api/vet</code>, <code>/api/visit</code>, <code>/api/customer</code> and <code>/api/genai</code>. The routes live in the api-gateway module's own application.yml, not in the config repo's api-gateway.yml.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:22",
            "quote": "uri: lb://vets-service"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:40",
            "quote": "uri: lb://genai-service"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Every gateway route has a default CircuitBreaker filter that forwards to <code>/fallback</code>, which answers 503.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:14",
            "quote": "fallbackUri: forward:/fallback"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/boundary/web/FallbackController.java:15",
            "quote": "HttpStatus.SC_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The gateway serves the Vue index.html for browser (text/html) navigation that is not under /api, /actuator, /webjars or /fallback.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/ApiGatewayApplication.java:66",
            "quote": "new ClassPathResource(\"static/index.html\")"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/ApiGatewayApplication.java:72",
            "quote": "RequestPredicates.path(\"/api/**\").negate()"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Gateway, customers-service and visits-service read their configuration from the Config server on port 8888 (<code>CONFIG_SERVER_URL</code>, default localhost; <code>config-server</code> host under the docker profile).",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:5",
            "quote": "optional:configserver:${CONFIG_SERVER_URL:http://localhost:8888/}"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-customers-service/src/main/resources/application.yml:13",
            "quote": "configserver:http://config-server:8888"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-visits-service/src/main/resources/application.yml:13",
            "quote": "configserver:http://config-server:8888"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The gateway is fixed at port 8080 in all profiles; under the docker profile customers-service (8081) and visits-service (8082) get fixed ports and all register with Eureka at discovery-server:8761. By default services use a random port.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:api-gateway.yml:5",
            "quote": "port: 8080"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:customers-service.yml:16",
            "quote": "port: 8081"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:visits-service.yml:16",
            "quote": "port: 8082"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:visits-service.yml:20",
            "quote": "defaultZone: http://discovery-server:8761/eureka/"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:5",
            "quote": "port: 0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The only time limit configured in the gateway is <b>10 seconds</b>, set as the default for its circuit breakers (the default Resilience4j configuration; no per-breaker setting or <code>resilience4j.*</code> property exists in either repo). The browser gives up after 15 seconds. On the chat route a timeout ends in a 503 from <code>/fallback</code>, and the chat box then shows its own \"Chat is currently unavailable\" message. On the owner page the 10 seconds cover only the visits call (the customers call before it has no limit); on timeout the visits fall back to an empty list, so an owner shows without visits and no error.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/ApiGatewayApplication.java:88",
            "quote": "timeoutDuration(Duration.ofSeconds(10))"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/ApiGatewayApplication.java:86",
            "quote": "factory.configureDefault(id -> new Resilience4JConfigBuilder(id)"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml:45",
            "quote": "CircuitBreaker=name=genaiCircuitBreaker,fallbackUri=/fallback"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/boundary/web/FallbackController.java:15",
            "quote": "HttpStatus.SC_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/boundary/web/ApiGatewayController.java:60",
            "quote": "cbFactory.create(\"getOwnerDetails\")"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/api/boundary/web/ApiGatewayController.java:61",
            "quote": "cb.run(it, throwable -> emptyVisitsForPets())"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/static/scripts/api/client.js:1",
            "quote": "const REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS = 15000;"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/static/scripts/components/ChatBox.js:56",
            "quote": "content: 'Chat is currently unavailable'"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-api-gateway/src/main/resources/static/scripts/api/client.js:82",
            "quote": "throw new ApiError(`Request failed ("
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "group": "Data",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "By default each of customers-service and visits-service uses its own embedded HSQLDB, initialised from <code>db/hsqldb/schema.sql</code> and <code>data.sql</code>; the shared default config sets no JDBC URL. The <code>mysql</code> profile in the shared config switches to a MySQL schema and data scripts.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:13",
            "quote": "schema-locations: classpath*:db/hsqldb/schema.sql"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:14",
            "quote": "data-locations: classpath*:db/hsqldb/data.sql"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:98",
            "quote": "on-profile: mysql"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:105",
            "quote": "schema-locations: classpath*:db/mysql/schema.sql"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-customers-service/pom.xml:71",
            "quote": "<artifactId>hsqldb</artifactId>"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-visits-service/pom.xml:64",
            "quote": "<artifactId>hsqldb</artifactId>"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Hibernate does not create tables (<code>ddl-auto: none</code>); schema comes from the SQL scripts.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:27",
            "quote": "ddl-auto: none"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Under the <code>mysql</code> profile the datasource settings live once, in the shared config. No service has its own datasource setting, and customers, visits, vets and genai-service all ship the MySQL driver, so every one of them that takes the shared config uses the same database. docker-compose.yml defines eleven services (config, discovery, customers, visits, vets, genai, api-gateway, tracing, admin, grafana, prometheus) and none is a database; the image sets the <code>docker</code> profile, not <code>mysql</code>.",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices-config:application.yml:98",
            "quote": "on-profile: mysql"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-customers-service/pom.xml:66",
            "quote": "<artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-visits-service/pom.xml:73",
            "quote": "<artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-vets-service/pom.xml:94",
            "quote": "<artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker/Dockerfile:14",
            "quote": "SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=docker"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:spring-petclinic-genai-service/pom.xml:107",
            "quote": "<artifactId>mysql-connector-j</artifactId>"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:2",
            "quote": "config-server:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:17",
            "quote": "discovery-server:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:35",
            "quote": "customers-service:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:50",
            "quote": "visits-service:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:65",
            "quote": "vets-service:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:81",
            "quote": "genai-service:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:101",
            "quote": "api-gateway:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:116",
            "quote": "tracing-server:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:126",
            "quote": "admin-server:"
          },
          {
            "ref": "spring-petclinic-microservices:docker-compose.yml:143",
            "quote": "grafana-server:"
          },
